{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Command the children of Israel, that they give to the Levites, from the inheritance of their possession, cities to dwell in, and open land for the cities around them.</b> The term מגרש means open space — an unbuilt area outside the city, surrounding it, to serve as an adornment for the city, from the city wall outward a thousand cubits around. They are not permitted to build a house there, or plant a vineyard, or sow a sowing; rather, it is for their animals, their property, and all their beasts."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:52.248783861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}